Key Takeaways

Phone number as session key is the correct memory design for WhatsApp agents.
It isolates each user's conversation context without requiring authentication or
user registration.
Intent normalization before tool-calling eliminates the most common failure
mode in conversational agents: ambiguous inputs producing bad tool queries.
Always normalize to a controlled vocabulary before hitting external data sources.
Google Sheets as a live knowledge base tool gives clients direct control over
content without workflow access. Separating content from logic is good practice
for any production deployment where the client needs to update information
independently.
Fallback behavior for tool failures is non-negotiable in customer-facing agents.
Silent failures (empty responses, error messages) destroy trust. Always define what
the agent does when a tool returns nothing.
CRM logging after send (not in parallel) ensures lead records only exist for
successfully completed interactions — keeping data quality high without additional
deduplication logic.
